From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(NetworkSettings): a late password prompt only on
 the Network page

A join that fails for its password asks for it again (0018), up to 45 s
after it was given (90 polls of 0.5 s). With the Network page left by
then the dialog, a child of the hidden page, was not on the screen, but
its keyboard is OpenGamepadUI's one keyboard and opened over whatever
was: the main menu lost its focus to it, and B did nothing there until
Guide closed the menu; with Network the Settings page last shown, the
page also took the next B (MANGMI Air X, 2026-11-27, the prompt replayed
in a running OpenGamepadUI). The page checked its own `visible`, which
stays true when a parent hides it.

The prompt, its keyboard and the page's B handling now need the page on
the screen (is_visible_in_tree). A prompt that comes with the page left
is dropped; selecting the network asks again. Replayed the same way
after: no keyboard and B as usual with the page left; with the page on
the screen the dialog and its keyboard open as before.
---
diff --git a/core/ui/common/settings/network_settings_menu.gd b/core/ui/common/settings/network_settings_menu.gd
index f786824..d39beca 100644
--- a/core/ui/common/settings/network_settings_menu.gd
+++ b/core/ui/common/settings/network_settings_menu.gd
@@ -140,6 +140,11 @@ func _on_visible_changed() -> void:
 
 
 func _on_wifi_challenge(callback: Callable) -> void:
+	# A join can fail up to 45 s after its password was given, and asks again then: with this page
+	# left by then, the keyboard opened over whatever was on the screen, for a dialog that was not.
+	# The network's row keeps its "Check the password"; selecting it asks again.
+	if not is_visible_in_tree():
+		return
 	_close_dialog()
 	_dialog_ssid = wifi_tree.challenge_ssid
 	# The open network in use has no password: the dialog names it and offers Forget network.
@@ -203,7 +208,7 @@ func _close_dialog() -> void:
 
 ## Opens the on-screen keyboard on the password field, if its dialog is still up.
 func _open_keyboard() -> void:
-	if not password_popup.visible or not password_input.line_edit.visible:
+	if not is_visible_in_tree() or not password_popup.visible or not password_input.line_edit.visible:
 		return
 	password_input.keyboard.open(password_input.keyboard_context)
 
@@ -218,7 +223,7 @@ func _close_keyboard() -> void:
 # B closes the password dialog, one step at a time: the keyboard first (it closes itself on B and
 # consumes it), then the dialog.
 func _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
-	if not visible:
+	if not is_visible_in_tree():
 		return
 	if not password_popup.visible:
 		return
